import type { Unit } from "@/content/types";

// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// b2-unit-60-political-social-discourse — "The Language of Debate"
// Vocabulary-domain unit: no new grammar concept. Tier 2 reinforces
// congiuntivo (opinion, doubt, and concessive triggers), the indicative
// after certainty expressions, si-impersonale/passivante, relative pronouns
// (ciò che/quello che/il che/cui), comparativi/superlativi, passive voice,
// and futuro/condizionale — all already taught in the B1/B2 prerequisite
// chain — in fresh debate-themed context.
//
// Overlap check performed before writing (per CURRICULUM.md instruction):
// - b1-unit-42-politics-civic-basics.ts: covers the MECHANICS of voting and
//   local/national government (votare, il seggio, il sindaco, le urne,
//   la campagna elettorale, il primo ministro, la maggioranza/minoranza,
//   futuro/condizionale/imperfetto/si-impersonale/comparativi grammar built
//   around elections). It does not touch the RHETORIC of debate itself —
//   no discourse connectors, no argumentation vocabulary, no polarization
//   language. This unit deliberately does not re-teach any b1-42 word as a
//   new tier-1 card (dibattito, sondaggio, maggioranza, minoranza, partito,
//   schierarsi-con-un-partito already exist there) and only reuses "il
//   dibattito"/"la maggioranza"/"schierarsi" incidentally inside example
//   sentences the way any B2 unit reinforces earlier vocabulary — never as
//   its own tier-1 card here.
// - b2-unit-40-law-society.ts: covers legal/judicial institutions and
//   rights (la legge, il tribunale, la sentenza, l'imputato, il ricorso,
//   la costituzione, il parlamento, il governo, l'opposizione). It is about
//   the STRUCTURE of law and courts, not the language people use to argue
//   with each other. No tier-1 word overlaps; this unit's territory is
//   argumentation, rhetoric, consensus/dissent, and debate register
//   (a mio avviso, si potrebbe obiettare che, è innegabile che, da un
//   lato...dall'altro) — a different lexical field entirely.
// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

